<title>UK: GECC sets $250 million six-year Eurobond.</title>
<headline>GECC sets $250 million six-year Eurobond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue was announced by lead manager UBS Ltd.</p>
<p> BORROWER   GENERAL ELECTRIC CAPITAL CORP</p>
<p> AMT	  $250 MLN  COUPON     6.50	MATURITY    04.OCT.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.168    PAY DATE    04.OCT.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.275     REOFFER    99.168    SPREAD	+10 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  U.S.	TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.125     SELL CONC  0.15	PRAECIP     NONE</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND WHEN-ISSUED FIVE-YEAR U.S. T-NOTE</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
